<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">04062026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Syria's National Commission for the Missing has confirmed that all six children of the al-Abbasi family, vanished with their mother in twenty-thirteen, are dead.</s> <s>Investigators reached that conclusion from footage tied to the Tadamon massacre — no remains were ever recovered.</s> <s>A year after Assad's fall, the country is reconstructing its atrocities from video alone, and the families want names, not just findings.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>North Korea's stockpile of weapons-grade nuclear material has more than doubled in five years, Kim Jong Un announced after inspecting a new production plant.</s> <s>Fissile material is the true bottleneck in building a warhead, and Pyongyang says it's removing it, ordering what Kim called exponential growth.</s> <s>Two decades of denuclearization diplomacy have ended not in disarmament but in a sequenced timetable for more.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Bulldozers have entered a protected Adriatic marine park to clear ground for a one-point-six-billion-dollar resort backed by Jared Kushner.</s> <s>An Albanian conservation group says the project paves over wetlands and monk-seal habitat with no published permits, and the country's anti-corruption prosecutor has opened an inquiry.</s> <s>At stake is whether a US presidential family's venture can override the environmental law of a sovereign Adriatic state.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Egypt has given itself nine months to replace the United Nations refugee agency as the sole authority deciding who counts as a refugee.</s> <s>Bylaws issued a year late hand asylum decisions to a state committee, displacing the agency that serves millions of Sudanese and Syrian applicants.</s> <s>A refugee-law specialist warns the timeline is far too short, leaving people's safety in the hands of the very state they fled toward.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Lagos, filmmakers and journalists are gathering for the fifth Africa International Human Rights Film Festival under the theme Stories of Resistance.</s> <s>As civic space contracts across the continent, the festival bets that cinema can document what legal crackdowns and censorship work to bury.</s> <s>It frames Africa's creators not as subjects of someone else's lens but as authors holding power to account.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Germany has lost its bid for a rotating Security Council seat, beaten by Portugal and Austria in the General Assembly vote.</s> <s>Berlin's foreign minister blamed Russian lobbying over its support for Ukraine, but the rejection of a G7 economy says more about shifting goodwill.</s> <s>These rotating seats carry a voice and little power — real authority still rests with the five permanent members and their vetoes.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>India's cabinet has approved a ten-thousand-crore-rupee fund letting state oil firms supply jet fuel at fixed prices.</s> <s>Fuel costs have risen two and a half times since March as the Iran war and shipping disruption squeeze supply, and the subsidy shields carriers from the spike.</s> <s>Airlines must buy from state suppliers for three years — a sign of how a war two thousand kilometres away reaches every Indian balance sheet.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Cuba suspends all Visa and Mastercard transactions from the sixth of June, after a foreign intermediary cut off its card processing.</s> <s>The central bank ties the move to a US executive order on the first of May that broadened sanctions, and hotels, airlines, and shipping firms are already pulling out.</s> <s>For an island that runs on tourist cash, losing the cards those tourists carry is its own kind of blockade.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's Oil and Gas Development Company has struck two thousand barrels a day at a well called Bobi Deep One in Sindh.</s> <s>The country's fuel imports drain its current account, so any domestic find eases pressure on a fragile balance of payments.</s> <s>The company confirms the reservoir's potential but has set no production date — promise, for now, without a timeline.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>China's carbon dioxide emissions rose two percent in the first quarter of this year, not despite its record renewable build-out but partly because of it.</s> <s>Grid operators wasted wind and solar power rather than throttle back coal, pushing power-sector emissions up four percent.</s> <s>With a super El Niño forecast to cut hydro output, the lesson is that clean capacity means little until the grid can actually carry it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>New seafloor measurements may sharpen earthquake warnings for southern Japan, where the Philippine Sea Plate grinds against the mainland at the Nankai Trough.</s> <s>Tracking imperceptible creep on the ocean floor reveals how stress quietly builds in the years before a rupture.</s> <s>A great megathrust there could threaten millions, and reading how the strain accumulates is the first step toward catching its warning signs.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The five-thousand-three-hundred-year-old gut of Ötzi the Iceman still holds living bacteria, researchers in Bolzano report.</s> <s>They found both ancient and modern strains, and the hard part is separating what's authentic from contamination introduced since his discovery in nineteen-ninety-one.</s> <s>If the older microbes prove genuine, Ötzi's gut could map the human microbiome as it was in the Copper Age.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Meta will now let employees switch off its workplace tracking — for up to thirty minutes at a time.</s> <s>The company logs keystrokes to train its AI models, and after a fifteen-hundred-signature petition it offered this pause, not an opt-out right.</s> <s>What the half-hour cap reveals is a surveillance default so normalised that a brief reprieve passes for a concession.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A Canadian startup called Ursa Ag has built a no-software tractor that costs half of a comparable John Deere and carries no digital repair locks.</s> <s>More than a thousand farmers in thirty countries reached out after its debut, echoing a hunger for the repairable machines of decades past.</s> <s>The company is tripling production — a small revolt against equipment you own but aren't allowed to fix.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Britain has forced Google to let publishers opt out of its AI Overviews without losing their ordinary search rankings.</s> <s>Google controls more than ninety percent of UK search, so being fed into its AI answers has been effectively mandatory until now.</s> <s>The competition regulator's move is a test of whether publishers can survive the AI summaries that quietly absorb their work.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>